{"id": "q0003", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 16, "onset_chunk": 16, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are 5 windows. Each window is 35 inches wide, so the total width of the windows is 5 times 35, which is 17 5 inches. Luke needs to buy fabric equal to two times the total width of the windows, so he should buy 2 times 175, which is 3 50 inches of fabric.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "q0007", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 21, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A basic manicure starts at $ 3", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "q0014", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 18, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "He had 60 apples. He ate two-fifths of them, which is 2 4, leaving him with 3 6. Then he gave his sister 25% of the remaining number, which is 9, leaving him with 2 7. So he sold these to his uncle at $3 each, so that's 2 7 times 3, which is $ 81. Answer: 8 1.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "q0021", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 25, "onset_chunk": 25, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Each middle shelf can hold 10 books, so the two middle shelves together can hold 20 books. The bottom shelf can hold twice as many as a middle shelf, so it can hold 2 0 books. The top shelf can hold 5 fewer books than the bottom shelf, so it can hold 1 5 books. So in total, one bookcase can hold 10 + 1 0 + 20 + 15 = 5 5 books. To find out how many book cases Ellie needs, we divide the total number of books by the number of books each bookcase can hold: 1 10 / 55 = 2. Therefore, El lie needs 2 book cases to hold all her books.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 37, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "q0027", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 17, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Alright, so let's figure this out. A ra has been on the team for 4 years, and she plays 4 0 games each year. That means over 4 years, she' s played a total of 4 times 40 games, which is 1 6 0 games. Each game, she scores 2 1 points. So to find her total points, we multiply the number of games by her points per game: 1 60 games times 2 1 points equals 3 3 60 points. So far in four years, Ara has scored 3 3 60 points.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 39, "carrier_ended": null}
