{"id": "q0244", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "n_q_chunks": 26, "onset_chunk": 25, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The initial horizontal speed is 3 0 m/s. After 4 seconds, the vertical speed due to gravity is g times time, which is 10 m/ s² times 4 seconds, equaling 40 m/s. Using the Pythagorean theorem, the total speed is the square root of 30 squared plus 40 squared, which is 50 m/s. So the answer is B.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
