{"id": "q0369", "pool": "easy-fact", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Venom is a substance that an animal injects into another organism, usually through bite s or stings. Poison, on the other hand, is something that is harmful if ing ested, inhaled, or absorbed through the skin. So venom is delivered actively, while poison is typically encountered pass ively.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
